Patch 0173: a buffer a client closes is handed out again instead of being allocated, wired and entered into the
GPU's tables, its pages go in a physical run at a time instead of 4 KB, and the imported pages are stored to
memory once per group of SUBMITs (boot-arg sweetmalistore=1: before every SUBMIT, as before).
The reuse is only for a buffer that had no mapping alive at the close (the kernel's retain count of its memory
is 1), it keeps the same GPU address (so the tables need no update), and it is zeroed before it goes out again.
Boot 2026-11-28: on the widget page a CREATE_BO cost 7.1 ms and a SUBMIT 310 us against 53 us at boot.

